[ceiling] The flat annulus at Z5.4 is the underside bearing seat for the M5×50 socket-head pivot screw: Ø9.2 head recess around a Ø5.6 through hole. It recesses the head above the base's flat bed-contact face. The seat has solid pedestal stock above it; the 1.8 mm radial span is an open head pocket, not a thin roof. Any automatically generated support here is reached through the underside Ø9.2 opening. Native support-contact review and removal are separate from this geometric access description.
alternatives: Omitting the recess leaves the socket head below the base and rocks the jig on the bench. A conical print-friendly seat removes the selected socket head's flat bearing surface and requires a different long countersunk screw. Loading the screw from above puts its retaining nuts below the flat base or requires an additional captured-nut feature.
