[thin] These two rankings join an end face of an 8 mm thick guide rail to an opposing face of a 4 mm long, 5 mm high seating stop. The branches are separated laterally by 0.2 mm and are each backed by the 8 mm base plate. The 2.024/2.026 mm nearest-face chords cross air in the analytic solid; they do not measure a material ligament. The stop's full axial section is 4 mm, and its ram-contact width is 14.5 mm.
alternatives: Joining each stop to its rail with additional shoulder stock removes this opposite-face pairing but adds material outside the ram-contact width without increasing a thin wall, because no wall exists along either reported chord. Moving the rail's front end back to the stop face also removes the pairing but shortens its alignment lead-in by 2 mm. The independent simple rectangular bearing members retain the specified fit clearances.
