[thin] These four instances are the two upper saddle cheeks at their minimum 2.9 mm radial stock, between the Ø32.2 drop-in pocket and the outer faces at Y±19. Stock grows thicker below this short upper band. The saddle locates the donor's robust round metal base with 0.35 mm radial loading clearance; the 12 mm axial thrust wall carries insertion reaction, and the tangent floor and flat column pad establish height and clocking. The cheek tips are not the axial thrust member. Geometry and solid native slicing do not establish physical load capacity.
alternatives: Increasing the outer half-width from 19 to 20.1 mm gives a 4 mm tip but grows the donor-side obstruction beyond the flush thrust-wall faces, including toward the attached faucet lever's open side, without enlarging the axial reaction wall. Reducing the saddle radius adds tip stock by consuming the 0.35 mm metal-loading clearance and risks binding the donor during placement and removal.
